{
  "dom_id": "step-q110601",
  "name": "Question 2",
  "problem": "Which of the following sets is a subspace of ${R}^{3}?$\n\nI. $A=\\{⟨x,y,z⟩\\in {R}^{3}:4x+5y-z=0\\}$\n\nII. $B=\\{⟨x,y,z⟩\\in {R}^{3}:{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+{z}^{2}=1\\}$\n\nIII. $C=\\{0\\}$",
  "worked_solution": "Let's analyze each of the subsets.\n\n- The set $A$ is a subspace. It represents a plane, and a plane is a subspace if and only if it passes through the origin. Here, the components of the zero vector $0=⟨0,0,0⟩$ satisfy the equation $4x+5y-z=0$ since $4\\cdot 0+5\\cdot 0-0=0.$ So $0$ lies in $A.$\n\n- The set $B$ is not a subspace because it does not contain the zero vector. Indeed, $0=⟨0,0,0⟩$ does not satisfy the condition ${x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+{z}^{2}=1$ since ${0}^{2}+{0}^{2}+{0}^{2}\\ne 1.$\n\n- The set $C$ is a subspace. This subset has only one element, the zero vector $0=⟨0,0,0⟩,$ which is a special subspace of ${R}^{3}.$\n\nIn conclusion, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\"",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
